{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/vignettes/realtime.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T15:58:58.926187Z","id":"18ebef6706263695ad5069b14dd60b00aa19585079da964f4e4fb38a91fe1d1d","body":{"detail":"The shell colours each peer's arrow and name tag by pick_color (crates/clax-core/src/live_layers.rs:239), whose preferred colour is a hash of the person's ID, and memberOf (web/e2e/hosted-helpers.ts) makes new people with fresh IDs on every run; two fast renders showed Mia in teal, then in red. The deterministic mode's byte-identical frames (plan Task 2, realtime_determinism) need the people's IDs, or the colours, fixed per run.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":77},"end":{"line":78},"content_hash":"ad9592accb8c5f3f34104706d7908901cc250c6e38657b1bdf872837a2b6e550"},"suggested_fix":"Find the source when realtime_determinism first fails: seed the people with fixed IDs if the daemon allows it, or make the colour a function of something the vignette fixes.","summary":"Mia's and Sam's live colours differ from run to run: a deterministic render of realtime will not be byte-identical as it stands","tags":["session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/vignettes/realtime.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T16:50:24.589423Z","id":"dce532c4f50587cd5116377c007a8b052bee8f8d82e6321c32f0f8a4911be965","body":{"detail":"pick_color (crates/clax-core/src/live_layers.rs:239-255) gives a person their preferred colour (a hash of their public ID) only when nobody in the room holds it, else the next free one: fixed IDs alone still give other colours if people join in another order, or if someone who holds a colour (the owner's setup page) is still in the room. The daemon mints public IDs at random (new_public_id, crates/clax-core/src/ids.rs) and no API takes one, so the reel fixes the colours without a daemon change: memberIn (web/reel/people.ts) mints invites until the person's public ID hashes (FNV-1a, as live_layers.rs fnv1a) to the colour asked for, revoking the others (DELETE /api/people/invites/{id} frees the name); realtime.ts setup moves Alex's setup page off the artifact before the invites, has Mia (colour 2, teal) and then Sam (colour 0, blue) join before the camera, and fails unless each one's live socket is welcomed in that colour. //web/reel:realtime_determinism: two recordings, 210 frames each, identical.","kind":"comment","references":"18ebef6706263695ad5069b14dd60b00aa19585079da964f4e4fb38a91fe1d1d","summary":"The colour also depends on join order, and the reel now fixes both: people minted to a colour, joining before the camera","tags":["reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/vignettes/realtime.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T16:50:26.131873Z","id":"4182b67dd13ed8e662848f8535ef69f55cac9dd5d6953c4e37390db4d363b9dc","body":{"detail":"Alex is the hosted daemon's first person, made by the setup page (ownerOf), not by an invite, so memberIn (web/reel/people.ts) cannot mint him to a colour. He joins after Mia and Sam, so he never takes theirs, and the camera films his own view, which draws no pointer or tag for him. A vignette that films someone else's view of the owner, or shows the owner's colour anywhere, has to fix it another way (for example a member as the owner's stand-in, or a daemon-side seed).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":139},"end":{"line":140},"content_hash":"1b8eea9030df5f9494cb44a50c7f27bbfc83eaa4f68834f416fc27d0ce47025c"},"summary":"Alex's own live colour is whatever is free when he joins, a different one each run; nothing on his own screen shows it in this vignette","tags":["reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/vignettes/realtime.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T16:57:36.797785Z","id":"ccfb5b0a1867af2d1cadfccdb1a84f8d0b6c3637e3afb3bd9c3a3cee103d8115","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:a3056efdc8764889eda4d9caef5c6a66f0ea071b","summary":"Fixed by a3056efdc: Mia and Sam are minted to live colours 2 and 0 (web/reel/people.ts memberIn) and join before the camera, which checks each welcome colour; bazelisk test //web/reel:realtime_determinism PASSED: 'realtime: two deterministic recordings, 210 frames each, identical'","supersedes":"18ebef6706263695ad5069b14dd60b00aa19585079da964f4e4fb38a91fe1d1d","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/vignettes/coldopen.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T17:34:42.822319Z","id":"26f6d71bde492a19f13c2c8a2d09654471cb24c1f3c53b18249b61b324e3bede","body":{"detail":"The daemon stamps real times and the camera's clock reads REEL_EPOCH (web/reel/camera.ts), so the gallery would read \"7 d ago\" for a page just published, varying by the day. restamp() rewrites every *_at time in the answers the route in setup() matches (/api/artifacts, /api/artifacts/<id>, /api/inbox, /api/inbox/summary): seeded pages to their SEEDS age, everything else to the film's now. A view that reads times from another endpoint, or from a stream delta, shows the daemon's real time instead; none is on screen in this vignette as filmed.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":44},"end":{"line":59},"content_hash":"aa1faaf16d572e731bca7704b2a3b967aaa84d03a351d344bb82a34ea0cde26c"},"summary":"The cold open's times are staged: the camera's artifact and inbox answers are restamped to the film's clock","tags":["reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/vignettes/coldopen.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T17:34:42.822425Z","id":"4da97bdc5741b50c2af01f66ae7f6215312204e3ff76dde9c641a6b6c1014ec6","body":{"detail":"The hosted gallery's header reads location.host (web/shell/src/ui/Gallery.svelte, `site`), so a port from freePort() made two deterministic recordings differ. setup() asks for PORT and falls back to a free port when it is taken (as when coldopen_fast and coldopen_frames are built at once): that recording is fine to look at, but //web/reel:coldopen_determinism fails on frame 000000 if anything else holds 47391 while it runs.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":84},"end":{"line":95},"content_hash":"182ea023ed4878e0995a25b5784bf8d1b3214250ce68cda12da5d36875dcf94b"},"suggested_fix":"Show a fixed public host in the header (a host-resolver rule mapping a name such as clax.dev to the daemon, in record.ts's Chromium flags), which would also make the header read as clax.dev.","summary":"The cold open's daemon runs on a fixed port (47391), since the gallery header shows host and port; a taken port changes that header","tags":["reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/vignettes/coldopen.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T18:59:51.778574Z","id":"1fdbfe7746b318499ac9a3f4460bc33e6b73a4bc3884dba0d1941def2224a639","body":{"detail":"The daemon stamps real times and has no injectable clock. setup() sets the camera page's clock LAG_MS (120 s) behind real time, so anything the film makes reads \"just now\" and the agent's elapsed clock 0:00 (relativeTime and clock() in web/shell/src clamp at zero); restamp() (coldopen.ts:61:76) rewrites the *_at times of the seeded pages, in the answers the route at :143:149 matches (/api/artifacts, /api/artifacts/<id>, /api/inbox, /api/inbox/summary), to fixed ages before that clock. A view that reads a seeded page's time from another endpoint or a stream delta shows the daemon's time (seconds ago, so \"just now\"). The shell's haiku is picked by Math.random (gallery footer) or by the working record's key, a fresh ULID each run (WorkingStrip.svelte), so the route at :157:163 serves the camera a one-item list (an entry of web/shell/src/view/haiku.json): the film's haiku is chosen, not drawn. The caret's blink, on the browser's own time, is held still by STILL_CARET (caret-animation: manual).","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":136},"end":{"line":163},"content_hash":"1be05644724d0cec2a302f0619be5ee3b8fc6fc67a7f6177a090f31210310db1"},"summary":"The cold open stages its times and haiku: the camera's clock runs 2 min behind real time, seeded pages' times are restamped, and the haiku list is cut to one","supersedes":"26f6d71bde492a19f13c2c8a2d09654471cb24c1f3c53b18249b61b324e3bede","tags":["reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/vignettes/coldopen.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T18:59:51.864542Z","id":"13166068dcb70acb32b6a6cbf492a81a722bad02f434f12129069f9959f4c6db","body":{"detail":"The hosted gallery's header reads location.host (web/shell/src/ui/Gallery.svelte, `site`), so a port from freePort() made two deterministic recordings differ. setup() asks for PORT and falls back to a free port when it is taken (as when coldopen_fast and coldopen_frames are built at once): that recording is fine to look at, but //web/reel:coldopen_determinism fails on frame 000000 if anything else holds 47391 while it runs.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":99},"end":{"line":110},"content_hash":"9b23c329b69cb8b74aa2c7bcd935269719f41e7921b0cf35e14f4974f92c0e47"},"suggested_fix":"Show a fixed public host in the header (a host-resolver rule mapping a name such as clax.dev to the daemon, in record.ts's Chromium flags), which would also make the header read as clax.dev.","summary":"The cold open's daemon runs on a fixed port (47391), since the gallery header shows host and port; a taken port changes that header","supersedes":"4da97bdc5741b50c2af01f66ae7f6215312204e3ff76dde9c641a6b6c1014ec6","tags":["reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/vignettes/agent.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T18:59:09.259046Z","id":"4d6c1eda562479e3a4fd8e5a4c3455b1ad742e408e860f556506105bab476f01","body":{"detail":"pick_color (crates/clax-core/src/live_layers.rs) gives a joining person their hashed colour only when free; a page that navigates opens its new socket before the daemon has handled the old one's close. Up to five rejoins, offstage (no frame passes). After rejoining, the vignette also waits for her frame to hear `here` (the HERE init script) before moving her pointer: a move before that is never reported, and the glide waited 30 s.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":283},"end":{"line":296},"content_hash":"76ca606da4231fd739acfdc2251475f4518e91200382184fd106654c81f6b674"},"suggested_fix":"Have the daemon release a person's colour to that person's new socket, or close the old socket before the new one joins.","summary":"Mia's rejoin on version 2 retries until the daemon welcomes her in teal: her old live-layers socket can still hold the colour when her new one joins","tags":["reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/vignettes/agent.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T18:59:09.259080Z","id":"0542657b55559b6d702aaa24893bab75a4651acdb4a855cad1ab2aabd604db3c","body":{"detail":"A look sent after the publish counts as having seen version 2's address, so the thread lands under Open/Detached instead of \"Addressed in v2\" (seen in a deterministic render). The vignette holds frames in 100 ms steps until the look's answer arrives; a change to LOOK_EVERY_MS (web/shell/src/view/artifact-controller.ts:207) or to when the shell looks changes the frame count of the working beat.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":199},"end":{"line":244},"content_hash":"1e1b8c5a4a0a1fd26054623fd71550499d74cc789a6c708c0637432c5407834f"},"summary":"The agent publishes only after Alex's view has marked his thread looked at (PUT /api/viewers/me/looked), which the shell sends a second after a look on the page's clock","tags":["reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/vignettes/agent.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T18:59:09.259104Z","id":"6882fd70a33ea58722a931d1b1b6bf9b65c817e3f3da86072e080d6639252b17","body":{"detail":"After Mia rejoins version 2 her new socket can report a place of its own as it opens, and that report arrived before or after the glide's first step from run to run, which moved her drawn pointer on frames 298-303 between two renders. Nothing names the moment her last report has reached Alex, so the vignette waits for quiet. Her page's arrival animations are also waited out (document.getAnimations, line 302) because a place on a bar still sweeping in is told to Alex as a share of a box that differs from run to run.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":306},"end":{"line":320},"content_hash":"ddb390d2de6f2ef9b4e83f3fc6978b8eb7260c55c4d26142c1dd55d6719b2e35"},"suggested_fix":"Expose the sequence number of a peer's last cursor report to the frame (clax:peers), so the recorder waits for the report its move caused.","summary":"Before Mia's glide the vignette waits, in real time, until what Alex's view heard of her pointer has not changed for SETTLED_MS (500 ms): a stability heuristic, not a named state","tags":["reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/vignettes/game.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T19:52:40.263204Z","id":"1fad244bfdfcba9acb490e756376de5ce40118f6ac8c34c66d1b832ab8052b39","body":{"detail":"CAMERA_STYLE (installed on the camera's context at web/reel/vignettes/game.ts:192) sets `small.el`, `.thread-card .st.ag > small` and `.thread-card .waiting` to display: none, and `transition: none` on every element of the shell's top document. The elapsed clocks count from the daemon's real started_at to the camera page's fixed clock (web/reel/camera.ts pauses it near REEL_EPOCH, 2026-11-03), so they read about 158 hours and differ from run to run; the shell's transitions (a thread card's hover border, the Comment button leaving comment mode) were filmed at different ages in two runs of //web/reel:game_determinism. The film therefore differs from the real UI there: no elapsed time beside \"claude: Building a multiplayer star-chase\", no waiting line between Send and the agent taking the thread, and no fades. A daemon clock the recorder could set (or working views stamped on the page's clock) would let the film show them.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":66},"end":{"line":83},"content_hash":"e8aa13721ebff656ec2b379a7577ee61d80f947de575d784d0e1fc4232eac422"},"summary":"The game vignette's camera hides the shell's working elapsed clocks and the thread's \"sent, waiting\" line, and turns off the shell's CSS transitions","tags":["session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/vignettes/game.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T19:52:40.263257Z","id":"646b1301102505fe432f5ccef334fbf3ca905a4c9fc435765b7399ddabe1d6a7","body":{"detail":"`delete globalThis.SharedWorker` (web/reel/vignettes/game.ts:191) makes web/shell/src/stream.ts bestLink fall back from workerLink. With the shared worker, Reload (a full shell load mid-film) fetched stream-worker-*.js again and the deterministic camera's quiet() in web/reel/camera.ts waited 10 s on that request and failed the recording (\"a frame waited 10 s on .../_clax/shell/stream-worker-*.js\"). The fallback looks the same on screen; it is still not the transport a person's browser uses. Teaching web/reel/camera.ts's `endless` to skip a shared worker's script request would remove the need.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":186},"end":{"line":192},"content_hash":"1d695b391478933ccd021efdc69f186edc2a22301c25bd28c2f2ccd61c6dcc29"},"summary":"The game vignette's camera browser has no SharedWorker, so its shell reads the event stream through the leader-link fallback","tags":["session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/vignettes/globe.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T19:46:24.370963Z","id":"9ff2678550a70ebec37127c49846778a1d0f5bcdd35887b3763c0387488c20f0","body":{"detail":"The camera installs the page clock at REEL_EPOCH (2026-11-03T09:41Z, web/reel/camera.ts) while the daemon stamps comments, working records and look marks on the wall clock, so relativeTime (web/shell/src/format.ts) reads '7 d ago', the working clock (web/shell/src/view/working-model.ts) reads '158:50:17', and both differ between two recordings by however long setup took. FILM_TIMES wraps window.fetch in the camera's top document: every ISO time in /api/artifacts*, /api/viewers/me/looked and the /api/stream body becomes the page's now as it arrives, and SharedWorker is removed so the page holds its own stream. Every vignette that shows a daemon time needs the same; the coldopen vignette restamps GET answers by route for the same reason. A daemon test clock (debug builds) set to the film's time, or a shared restamp in record.ts, would serve all of them.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":42},"end":{"line":89},"content_hash":"d143bade95ca7f5029f981546c215fdc689ccc2ae12a18badafedf21af786787"},"summary":"Daemon times are restamped in the camera's page because REEL_EPOCH is a week ahead of the daemon's wall clock","tags":["status:needs-decision","reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/vignettes/globe.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T19:46:24.371024Z","id":"ffb5e34ed8e6481b2de6aa5b0c15bcd9df73b3faad9b6629c48f265eac895997","body":{"detail":"A text caret blinks on the browser's real time, not the stepped clock: two deterministic recordings differed only where the composer's caret was shown in one and blinked off in the other. A new thread's card is selected when its post is answered, and the stream's copy of the thread may render it first, unselected, in one run and not the other, so its border transition ran in one run only. STILL (caret-color: transparent on fields, transition: none on .thread-card) is injected into the camera's top document. A camera-level answer (this style in record.ts for every deterministic camera, or a Chromium caret-blink setting) would serve every vignette that types or posts on camera.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":91},"end":{"line":95},"content_hash":"a364782f73df044c022bf34b619da2a1e8c5fccf09a0ead2e05add65e40a54d3"},"summary":"The camera's page draws no text caret and no thread-card transition: both would differ between recordings","tags":["reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/vignettes/globe.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T19:46:24.371053Z","id":"8ae43a66e27637a352e45f393d92d3ded89d1e6271808c0ad2a6dcb850d32407","body":{"detail":"deterministicCamera's freeze reaches every frame in page.frames() each roll (web/reel/camera.ts, reach), and fails with 'no frame ...' on one being detached or not yet in the frame tree: the old content frame during the Reload to v2, and the about:srcdoc frame the shell draws an area's clip in. drag() and press() hold the film still from the release until the state the click starts has landed (the composer focused with its clip and the srcdoc frame gone; v2's frame loaded and v1's gone), which also lands asynchronous UI (the card's selection, the composer's focus transition) on the same frame each run. Director.click rolls 150 ms right after the release, so any vignette whose click navigates the content frame or opens the composer on an area hits the same failure.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":99},"end":{"line":126},"content_hash":"6026d836f197db9279d4049aecfcfb6fc924b9510772fbf85ce1fe65628e728b"},"summary":"The camera fails on a frame that is coming or going: clicks that start one are pressed off camera and waited out","tags":["reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/vignettes/claxbot.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T17:46:40.068367Z","id":"b3fa3f0f43319a5cc5775781767f77d8d9236e54a96488049494d6d1b18a2cb6","body":{"detail":"bazelisk test //web/reel:claxbot_determinism fails (297 frames each, 78 differ). From the first finished script card on (frame 228 on), the run panel prints each script's wall-clock call time (web/shell/src/bot/RunPanel.svelte callsLine, '2 calls · 2 ms' in one run, '3 ms' in another), which the daemon measures (crates/clax-bot/src/script.rs, the call's ms). Scattered frames while typing in the New dialog (000030, 000036, 000037, 000042, …) differ by the text caret, whose blink runs on the browser's real time and which Page.captureScreenshot (web/reel/camera.ts) captures. Options: the camera hides the caret for every vignette (as Playwright's page.screenshot does by default with caret: 'hide'); and the daemon reports a call's ms through an injected clock, or the vignette ends on frames without the panel's call times.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":251},"end":{"line":260},"content_hash":"69288a5c2991c40239cc7dbb1d6bdf7e7d428dd534fb67da92334dc3bb783608"},"summary":"Two deterministic recordings of claxbot differ: ClaxBot's measured call times, and the text caret's blink","tags":["reel","determinism","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/vignettes/claxbot.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T17:46:40.068434Z","id":"a5843d9cb1a4b6eb0b560983ef5d9639bc1ba1bd542d2bfb5994e047c9fb3467","body":{"detail":"Not taken: a hosted daemon reads no [bot] configuration and no instance key from the environment (crates/clax-server/src/core.rs local_bot), and its store takes only a public https base URL (clax_store::bot_settings::BaseUrlPolicy::Hosted), so ClaxBot cannot be pointed at the scripted Messages API on loopback. The worker has BaseUrlPolicy::HostedLoopbackForTests (crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs); the daemon has no such switch.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":10},"end":{"line":13},"content_hash":"f85699a27f47963d907d168e8abb632b8dfe32f91083b3735f8524b4e80a273a"},"summary":"Film ClaxBot on a hosted daemon, as clax.dev runs it","tags":["reel","revisit:a hosted daemon can take a loopback ClaxBot base URL for tests","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/vignettes/dash.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T19:40:25.027601Z","id":"eca5dd13e563e32387eca1a0fa3a94bae8ea0f45b3f126fd7ffe3ad9635f3a98","body":{"detail":"The daemon stamps real time and the camera's clock reads REEL_EPOCH (web/reel/camera.ts), so threads read '7 d ago' and the working clock shows a varying hours figure. RESTAMP maps every '*_at' and 'since' value in /api/ JSON answers and in the stream worker's port messages to the film's clock, order-preserving, kept in sessionStorage across the reload. It leans on shell internals: the SharedWorker port path of web/shell/src/stream.ts and the shell comparing ISO strings (look marks in artifact-controller.ts look()). A shell change there can make the film read wrong (a restamp that ties two times dropped the 'Addressed in v2' group in an earlier draft) without failing the recording. A daemon clock the recorder could set would replace it.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":45},"end":{"line":87},"content_hash":"689fee5b0c6dc0d1d74ccd4beef84320aa331519d2621c735e2f54e1bb686109"},"summary":"RESTAMP rewrites the daemon's times inside the camera's shell by patching window.fetch and MessagePort message handlers","tags":["reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/vignettes/dash.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T19:40:25.027662Z","id":"cd9f55180f9bbc2ec2385c78a2a8a975403e3bcae0ae8bd2375d7628437c6821","body":{"detail":"web/shell/src/view/artifact-controller.ts look() marks a viewed thread looked one LOOK_EVERY_MS after it changes; v2's publish changes the thread, and if that mark is sent before the reload, the thread is no longer 'addressed' and v2 opens with it under Detached and no reply visible. The vignette parks the pointer by where Reload shows and holds 150 ms, so the press lands well inside the second; a longer hold or travel there breaks the reveal silently. The reload's release is also off camera (pressThen) because web/reel/camera.ts reach() throws 'no frame ... in ...' when freeze() meets the detaching v1 frame mid-navigation.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":200},"end":{"line":222},"content_hash":"9584eb1fff8ec33b31e696031f470e468f237c35d2814f5cc09f95947b49870e"},"summary":"The Addressed-in-v2 opening depends on Alex clicking Reload within LOOK_EVERY_MS (1 s of page time) of the publish","tags":["reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
